1086:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
1087:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  This function is used to send a connection request to the remote device with
1088:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  the connection parameters set in the BLE Component customizer. This function
1089:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  needs to be called only once after the target device is discovered by
1090:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  Cy_BLE_GAPC_StartScan() and further scanning has stopped. Scanning is
1091:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  successfully stopped on invoking Cy_BLE_GAPC_StopScan() and then receiving the
1092:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  event #CY_BLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_START_STOP with sub-parameter 'success' = 0x01u.
1093:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
1094:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  On successful connection, the following events are generated at the GAP
1095:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  Central device (as well as the GAP Peripheral device), in the following order.
1096:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  * #CY_BLE_EVT_GATT_CONNECT_IND
1097:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  * #CY_BLE_EVT_GAP_DEVICE_CONNECTED - If the device connects to a GAP Central and
1098:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    Link Layer Privacy is disabled.
1099:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  * #CY_BLE_EVT_GAP_ENHANCE_CONN_COMPLETE - If the device connects to a GAP Central and
1100:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    Link Layer Privacy is enabled.
1101:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  * #CY_BLE_EVT_GAP_DEVICE_CONNECTED
1102:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
1103:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  A procedure is considered to have timed out if a connection response packet is
1104:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  not received within time set by cy_ble_connectingTimeout global variable
1105:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  (30 seconds by default). #CY_BLE_EVT_TIMEOUT event with #CY_BLE_GENERIC_APP_TO parameter
1106:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  will indicate about connection procedure timeout. Connection will automatically
1107:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  be canceled and state will be changed to #CY_BLE_STATE_ON.
1108:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
1109:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  \param address: The device address of the remote device to connect to.
